Z||000000||tripstaatnod||09-23-2001||11:31 PM||||I bought a 85 GT about 6 months ago. It ran and had pretty good interrior but the rings were going or gone. one day I forgot to check the oil before I left the house and spun a bearing. I got another 85 GT parts car and I'm trying to make my car look good but When I got the car the Leather on the steering wheel what twisted like if some one grabbed it at the top and rotated their hand backwards. It will go back but it's stretched out. What can I do to fix this? Do I have to replace it? Can I just soak it in hot water?||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-24-2001||12:14 AM||||No theres nothing you can do except maybe send it to FieroDave to be refinished or the Fierostore used to do it. <BR>Its a common prob w/ Fiero steering wheels. Most leather ones Ive seen have the same prob...it comes w/ usage and age.<BR>The Fierostore actually sells new GT leather steering wheels (repro, but the look identical) for $150 I think. Im gonna put in in leu of my 4 spoker in my 86 Se.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
